# Dev-server-only convenience (DESIGN_DECISIONS.md D34). `npm run dev`
# reads this and injects it via vite.config.ts's define block so the owner
# doesn't have to open the in-app configuration menu on their own machine.
#
# This is NOT how players get a key: bring-your-own-key is the default
# path. Every player (including you, on any device but this one) adds
# their own Gemini API key in the configuration menu (the gear icon in the
# header) - it's stored in that browser's localStorage only, never sent
# anywhere but Google, never saved into a game file, and never bundled
# into `npm run build`'s output.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own key to use this convenience.
#
# Windows alternative (no plaintext file): leave this empty (or have no
# .env at all) and store the key as a GENERIC credential in Windows
# Credential Manager under the target name `GloryOfRome:GEMINI_API_KEY`:
#   cmdkey /generic:GloryOfRome:GEMINI_API_KEY /user:api /pass:<your key>
# (or Control Panel > Credential Manager > Windows Credentials > Add a
# generic credential). The dev server reads it at startup; a filled-in
# .env value takes priority over the credential. Same D34 boundary:
# dev server only, never in build output.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
